// Lesson 7.2 — Tile Collision, Layers & Sorting
// The Platformer scene's `Collision` tilemap ALREADY carries TilemapCollider2D
// (Composite Operation: Merge), CompositeCollider2D and a Static Rigidbody2D.
// Tilemap collision already works. This lesson is about USING and TUNING it:
// the physics layers, the 6.2 ground-check mask, sorting, and one-way platforms.
//
// Scaffolding: OUTLINE ONLY (level 3), and a BUILD lesson — there is no new
// script to write, so it keeps the code chip on the ask banner (do NOT pass the
// `concept` frame). The ask banner is the level marker: a level-3 lesson must
// not render a walkthrough, and verify-site refuses one that does (the
// `level >= 3 && wt` rule in scripts/verify-site.mjs).
//
// WHY THIS IS THE RUNG: the ladder is per concept, not per unit. 7.1 was the
// first treatment of painting; 7.2 is the same tileset again, asked to carry
// physics. The genuinely new idea is not a mechanism but a *classification* —
// "solid" and "decorative" are two jobs that one tilemap cannot hold, and
// "physics layer" and "sorting layer" are two lists with one word in common.
// Deciding which bucket a thing belongs in is a decision, which is what level 3
// is for.
//
// GROUND TRUTH (read out of AP_CS_P_Starter_Project, Unity 6000.6.0f1):
//   - Assets/_Scenes/{Start,Overworld,Platformer}.unity; EditorBuildSettings
//     gives Start 0, Overworld 1, Platformer 2.
//   - Platformer has exactly three tilemaps. `Collision` (tag `Ground`) and
//     `Cave Exit` (Untagged) EACH carry TilemapCollider2D
//     (m_CompositeOperation: 1 = Merge, m_UsedByEffector: 0), CompositeCollider2D
//     and a Rigidbody2D with m_BodyType: 2 = STATIC, m_GravityScale: 1.
//     The third, `No Collision`, has a TilemapRenderer and NO collider of any
//     kind — pure paint, so no raycast can ever hit it. (An earlier lesson
//     wrongly paired `Collision` with `No Collision`; that is not repeated.)
//   - THE LAYER TRAP, and the reason this file was rewritten. TagManager.asset
//     defines the tags Coin, Enemy, Axe, Spikes, Ground, GroundCheck — and the
//     project shipped with NO `Ground` LAYER at all (the first empty user layer
//     is index 8; the only named user layers are the placeholders "Layer 1/2/3"
//     at indices 20-22). 6.2 is the lesson where the student CREATES the Ground
//     layer and puts `Collision` and `Cave Exit` in it, so by 7.2 it exists —
//     but the failure mode of a mask naming a layer that does not exist is
//     silent and is NOT what this page used to say. `LayerMask.GetMask("Ground")`
//     logs an error and returns an EMPTY mask — it does not widen to everything
//     — so the ground check reads false on a floor you can see and the player
//     jumps in mid-air forever. An unset Inspector LayerMask is `Nothing`, which
//     is the same silence by another route. The old text claimed the mask
//     "defaulted to everything"; that was wrong and is fixed below.
//   - CORRECTED IN THIS REWRITE: the old Step 1 said "There is no Ground layer
//     in this project" while the old Step 2 said "You already created Ground
//     back in 6.2" — a flat self-contradiction. Both halves are now true: the
//     project SHIPPED without it, and 6.2 is where it gets made.
//   - Also corrected: the ground-check callout used to say one of the objects
//     answering a Default-mask raycast in the Platformer scene "can shoot".
//     Nothing in that scene shoots — it contains one prefab instance (the
//     Player), the three tilemaps, Main Camera, a Quad backdrop (a 3D
//     MeshCollider, invisible to Physics2D) and `Cave Exit`. Turrets live in
//     the Overworld. The line now describes what is actually there.
//   - Sorting layers are literally named Default, Bottom, Layer 2, Player,
//     Layer 4, Top. `Layer 2`/`Layer 4` are an unrenamed wart pending an editor
//     rename; this page teaches them as they are and asks the student what a
//     placeholder name costs.
//   - Physics2DSettings.asset: m_QueriesStartInColliders: 1, m_QueriesHitTriggers: 1,
//     m_Gravity: {x: 0, y: -9.81}.
//   - Player.prefab and Turret.prefab carry NO Collider2D and NO Rigidbody2D.
//     Turret.prefab and Turret_Projectile.prefab are BOTH tagged `Enemy`.
