const body = `<h1>7.2 — Tile Collision, Layers &amp; Sorting</h1>

<p class="lesson-lead">
    Your cave is already solid. You did not make it solid, and until today you could not have
    explained <em>why</em> it is solid. That is the uncomfortable part: three components are
    quietly doing heavy work under your feet, and a fourth thing — a project-wide list of
    layers your own code from <a href="6.2.html">6.2</a> is already gambling on — was never
    finished. Today you find out what you inherited, and you finish what you started.
</p>

${renderAskBanner('why is my tilemap solid, and why is my player in front of it?', 3)}

${renderDecompose('7.2', DECOMPOSE, 3)}

